dc:description>In its first part, the parchment manuscript contains the text that has been named, on the basis of its outstanding cycle of illustrations, the Aurora consurgens. The manuscript also contains numerous other alchemical treatises, for ex. Albertus Magnus on Secreta Hermetis philosophi, Johannes de Garlandia (John of Garland), excerpts from Geber (Jabir ibn Hayyan), the Thesaurus philosophiae and the Visio Arislei. Nine other Aurora-manuscripts are currently known to exist: Berlin Die uffgehnde Morgenrödte, Bologna, Glasgow, Leiden, Vienna, Paris, Prague and Venice. The Berlin manuscript, dating from the early sixteenth century and containing the illustrations as well as the texts in German translation, is closely related to the Zürich Codex.</dc:description><dc:format>100 ff., 20.4 x 13.9 cm</dc:format><dc:identifier>doi:10.5076/e-codices-zbz-Ms-Rh-0172</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/zbz/Ms-Rh-0172</dc:identifier><dc:identifier>Zürich, Zentralbibliothek, Ms. Rh. 172</dc:identifier><dc:publisher>e-codices - Virtual Manuscript Library of Switzerland</dc:publisher><dc:language>Latin</dc:language><dc:relation>Mohlberg Leo Cunibert, Katalog der Handschriften der Zentralbibliothek Zürich I, Mittelalterliche Handschriften, Zürich 1952, S. 246-248. Mit Korrekturen von Marlis Stähli, Zentralbibliothek Zürich. Literaturverzeichnis ergänzt.</dc:relation><dc:rights>e-codices / Zürich, Zentralbibliothek (cf. http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/about/terms)</dc:rights><dc:source rdf:resource="http://www.e-codices.unifr.ch/en/list/one/zbz/Ms-Rh-0172"></dc:source><dc:title>Zürich, Zentralbibliothek, Ms. Rh. 172 : Aurora consurgens</dc:title><dc:type>Manuscript</dc:type><dcterms:medium>Parchment</dcterms:medium><edm:europeanaProxy>false</edm:europeanaProxy><ore:proxyFor rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/item/9200211/en_list_one_zbz_Ms_Rh_0172"/><ore:proxyIn rdf:resource="http://data.europeana.eu/aggregation/provider/9200211/en_l